246
00:16:47,820 --> 00:16:48,820
Why are you still alive?

247
00:16:49,820 --> 00:16:52,820
Why are you here? You're supposed to be dead?

248
00:16:52,820 --> 00:16:59,820
What are you talking about? What made you think I was dead?

249
00:17:00,820 --> 00:17:01,820
Oh, I see.

250
00:17:02,820 --> 00:17:04,820
I guess that must have been another one of my nightmares.

251
00:17:05,820 --> 00:17:07,820
The delusions that come with the madness.

252
00:17:08,820 --> 00:17:12,820
Attacking me from the inside out until all of my lofty ideals crumble into dust.

253
00:17:13,820 --> 00:17:14,820
Stein!

254
00:17:15,820 --> 00:17:16,820
Please, Marie.

255
00:17:17,820 --> 00:17:18,820
Please get out of my sight.

256
00:17:18,820 --> 00:17:23,820
I don't know how much longer I can keep myself from dissecting you.

257
00:17:24,820 --> 00:17:25,820
No!

258
00:17:26,820 --> 00:17:27,820
Be careful.

259
00:17:27,820 --> 00:17:29,820
I wouldn't let that woman come any closer if I were you.

260
00:17:30,820 --> 00:17:31,820
Who knows what she might be planning?

261
00:17:32,820 --> 00:17:33,820
Oh.

262
00:17:34,820 --> 00:17:35,820
I do know.

263
00:17:36,820 --> 00:17:37,820
I know what she's capable of.

264
00:17:38,820 --> 00:17:40,820
I'm familiar with the skills she possesses.

265
00:17:41,820 --> 00:17:42,820
I've seen them.

266
00:17:43,820 --> 00:17:44,820
I've seen them all.

267
00:17:45,820 --> 00:17:46,820
Then let's take care of them together.

268
00:17:46,820 --> 00:17:48,820
The New World Order demands it of us.

269
00:17:49,820 --> 00:17:50,820
My handy vector blade.

270
00:17:53,820 --> 00:17:56,820
It was a cute little rebellion while it lasted, Krona, but it's all over now.

271
00:17:56,820 --> 00:18:12,820
Get back on your feet, idiot! If you die, so do I! I won't let that happen!

272
00:18:12,820 --> 00:18:13,820
Don't let that happen!

273
00:18:17,820 --> 00:18:19,820
This is what all that talk about killing me comes to in the end?

274
00:18:20,820 --> 00:18:21,820
Of course, I knew you wouldn't deliver.

275
00:18:22,820 --> 00:18:24,820
At least you provided me with some entertainment.

276
00:18:24,820 --> 00:18:32,820
Where am I?

277
00:18:33,820 --> 00:18:35,820
What path should I take?

278
00:18:36,820 --> 00:18:37,820
Move ahead?

279
00:18:38,820 --> 00:18:40,820
Join the new order that's waiting to be born?

280
00:18:40,820 --> 00:18:43,820
Or turn back to the old world?

281
00:18:44,820 --> 00:18:45,820
Am I still stable?

282
00:18:46,820 --> 00:18:49,820
Or am I being consumed by the madness?

283
00:18:50,820 --> 00:18:52,820
Is this the truth that I'm seeing?

284
00:18:53,820 --> 00:18:56,820
Or the fabricated delusions of insanity?

285
00:18:56,820 --> 00:19:02,820
Water ever flows from higher elevations down to lower ground.

286
00:19:03,820 --> 00:19:07,820
More and more water collects in one place, forming a river.

287
00:19:08,820 --> 00:19:11,820
So it is, too, with the lives of men.

288
00:19:12,820 --> 00:19:15,820
Set in their ways, they hate the loss of the old order.

289
00:19:16,820 --> 00:19:17,820
They fear change.

290
00:19:17,820 --> 00:19:19,820
But...

291
00:19:20,820 --> 00:19:22,820
What if it's better to fall from higher ground?

292
00:19:23,820 --> 00:19:24,820
To join the new river?

293
00:19:25,820 --> 00:19:28,820
Old or new, everything is controlled by the order.

294
00:19:29,820 --> 00:19:30,820
But that's okay.

295
00:19:31,820 --> 00:19:34,820
The only thing I need right now is...

296
00:19:37,820 --> 00:19:39,820
To obey the new rules.

297
00:19:39,820 --> 00:19:48,820
I'm begging you, Stein. Please, listen to me!

298
00:19:49,820 --> 00:19:52,820
I can't. There's something else I need to do at the moment.

299
00:19:53,820 --> 00:19:55,820
I'm going to cut you open now!

300
00:20:00,820 --> 00:20:01,820
What happened to your defiance?

301
00:20:02,820 --> 00:20:03,820
Throw it out!

302
00:20:04,820 --> 00:20:05,820
Now, Ragnarok!

303
00:20:06,820 --> 00:20:07,820
Go away!

304
00:20:09,820 --> 00:20:10,820
I know what you just did.

305
00:20:11,820 --> 00:20:13,820
You think hardening the black blood will make you safe?

306
00:20:14,820 --> 00:20:15,820
So wrong.

307
00:20:20,820 --> 00:20:22,820
Have you forgotten who you're dealing with?

308
00:20:23,820 --> 00:20:25,820
I'm the one who made you what you are in the first place.

309
00:20:32,820 --> 00:20:33,820
Wake up, moron!

310
00:20:34,820 --> 00:20:36,820
This isn't good! Pull yourself together!

311
00:20:39,820 --> 00:20:42,820
Go, bloody needle!

312
00:20:45,820 --> 00:20:46,820
It didn't...

313
00:20:46,820 --> 00:20:47,820
Oh, don't tell me you still haven't noticed.

314
00:20:48,820 --> 00:20:49,820
Let me explain it to you.

315
00:20:49,820 --> 00:20:51,820
You see, I hit you with my sole wavelength.

316
00:20:53,820 --> 00:20:58,820
Which, in turn, has made your wavelength significantly less stable, thereby rendering you virtually helpless.

317
00:20:58,820 --> 00:21:00,820
You can't even use bloody needle.

318
00:21:01,820 --> 00:21:04,820
And you will temporarily be unable to harden your blood.

319
00:21:05,820 --> 00:21:08,820
Which means it'll be very easy indeed for me to cut you into pieces.

320
00:21:09,820 --> 00:21:10,820
See it now?

321
00:21:10,820 --> 00:21:11,820
Now.

322
00:21:12,820 --> 00:21:13,820
This is the end.

323
00:21:14,820 --> 00:21:15,820
It's time you die!

324
00:21:15,820 --> 00:21:16,820
You die!

325
00:21:17,820 --> 00:21:18,820
You die!

326
00:21:19,820 --> 00:21:20,820
You die!

327
00:21:22,820 --> 00:21:23,820
You die!

328
00:21:26,820 --> 00:21:27,820
Oh!

329
00:21:30,820 --> 00:21:31,820
Medusa!

330
00:21:31,820 --> 00:21:57,740
so

331
00:22:01,820 --> 00:22:31,800
Thank you.

332
00:22:31,820 --> 00:23:01,800
Thank you.

333
00:23:01,820 --> 00:23:03,820
Thank you.

334
00:23:31,820 --> 00:23:33,320
Watch it or I'll...

335
00:23:33,320 --> 00:23:34,020
You'll what?

336
00:23:34,020 --> 00:23:34,380
No!

